1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:01,772
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,774 --> 00:00:02,988
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,529 --> 00:00:04,529
(Episode 22)

4
00:00:04,532 --> 00:00:06,455
- Have a seat.
- Thanks.

5
00:00:14,705 --> 00:00:16,486
Feeling a little better?

6
00:00:18,605 --> 00:00:20,754
I caused you trouble again.

7
00:00:20,978 --> 00:00:22,754
Of all times to run into you...

8
00:00:23,599 --> 00:00:24,611
I'm sorry.

9
00:00:26,431 --> 00:00:28,763
I wanted to take you to the beach,

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,434
but I thought it'd be better
to get somewhere nearby...

11
00:00:31,436 --> 00:00:33,649
and catch your breath.

12
00:00:34,265 --> 00:00:36,295
This was the only place I could think of.

13
00:00:38,227 --> 00:00:39,738
I like it here.

14
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,949
I can finally breathe.

15
00:00:42,358 --> 00:00:44,058
The beach is too far anyway.

16
00:00:45,396 --> 00:00:49,162
I liked those beach photos you showed me.

17
00:00:49,532 --> 00:00:52,150
You said the person you went with then...

18
00:00:52,152 --> 00:00:54,563
- was having a hard time, right?
- Yes.

19
00:00:54,745 --> 00:00:57,126
That person recently lost their spouse.

20
00:00:58,765 --> 00:01:00,134
Sa Bin,

21
00:01:00,574 --> 00:01:02,456
you must be an angel.

22
00:01:03,242 --> 00:01:04,564
Maybe to her...

23
00:01:07,031 --> 00:01:08,521
Is she a woman?

24
00:01:08,912 --> 00:01:11,334
- Could you kick the ball over?
- Sure.

25
00:01:15,003 --> 00:01:18,281
Yes, she's a woman.

26
00:01:19,102 --> 00:01:20,111
I see.

27
00:01:20,458 --> 00:01:21,459
Are you...

28
00:01:21,634 --> 00:01:23,781
- seeing her?
- No.

29
00:01:24,822 --> 00:01:26,507
I just admire her.

30
00:01:26,525 --> 00:01:28,862
Or, as people say these days,
I idolize her.

31
00:01:29,222 --> 00:01:30,236
"Idolize."

32
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:32,345
That's a nice word.

33
00:01:32,747 --> 00:01:33,758
Yes.

34
00:01:34,705 --> 00:01:36,912
I was glad I knew her husband well,

35
00:01:36,914 --> 00:01:40,941
but after he passed away, I find myself
worrying about her even more.

36
00:01:41,038 --> 00:01:43,585
I'm fine,
but I was worried I might burden her.

37
00:01:43,985 --> 00:01:45,722
You're very considerate.

38
00:01:46,431 --> 00:01:49,412
Since I've been on my own for so long,

39
00:01:49,415 --> 00:01:50,900
whenever I meet someone,

40
00:01:51,341 --> 00:01:54,377
I've developed a compulsion
to avoid any misunderstanding.

41
00:01:55,028 --> 00:01:56,341
I feel the same way.

42
00:01:57,025 --> 00:01:58,806
"Why don't you remarry?"

43
00:01:58,978 --> 00:02:00,961
"Why are you holding on like this?"

44
00:02:01,875 --> 00:02:03,407
There's no reason. I've just...

45
00:02:03,966 --> 00:02:07,049
gotten used to living this way
while raising my kids.

46
00:02:07,249 --> 00:02:08,265
Exactly.

47
00:02:08,865 --> 00:02:12,891
I've gotten used to living this way too.

48
00:02:17,785 --> 00:02:19,661
Just smile. Everything passes eventually.

49
00:02:20,629 --> 00:02:21,791
Yeah.

50
00:02:23,158 --> 00:02:26,010
- Sorry, could you kick it over here?
- Seriously...

51
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,614
The wind's blowing,
so why is it still so hot?

52
00:02:32,714 --> 00:02:34,647
Could you throw the ball over here?

53
00:02:34,971 --> 00:02:36,962
- Sure.
- Thank you!

54
00:02:38,173 --> 00:02:39,993
- Hey!
- Yes!

55
00:02:40,231 --> 00:02:42,885
- I told you to catch the ball!
- Come this way!

56
00:02:42,887 --> 00:02:44,088
Seriously!

57
00:02:47,472 --> 00:02:50,900
Feeling wronged is what
destroys people the most.

58
00:02:51,539 --> 00:02:52,877
You need to let it go.

59
00:02:52,974 --> 00:02:54,533
You did everything you could.

60
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:56,856
But it won't change anything.

61
00:02:56,965 --> 00:02:58,812
She won't even get a blood test.

62
00:02:59,565 --> 00:03:01,133
There's nothing we can do.

63
00:03:01,685 --> 00:03:05,090
I just had some hope
because she was so fond of O Reum.

64
00:03:08,172 --> 00:03:10,202
Let yourself be upset just for today.

65
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,854
Yes, just for today.

66
00:03:15,018 --> 00:03:17,852
You didn't have to walk me home,
but thank you.

67
00:03:18,018 --> 00:03:20,347
I haven't given you a singing lesson
in a while,

68
00:03:20,678 --> 00:03:23,559
but I'll start again
once things settle down.

69
00:03:23,714 --> 00:03:25,859
Okay, get some rest.

70
00:04:06,378 --> 00:04:07,506
O Reum,

71
00:04:08,747 --> 00:04:10,929
I did everything I could,

72
00:04:11,813 --> 00:04:13,540
but nothing came of it.

73
00:04:15,426 --> 00:04:16,740
What should I do?

74
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:28,506
Jung A.

75
00:04:28,637 --> 00:04:31,045
I'm leaving the country today.

76
00:04:32,185 --> 00:04:34,598
I'm not going to throw a party
or anything like that.

77
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,420
I'll just take care of business
and come right back.

78
00:04:36,525 --> 00:04:39,249
Why? Because of that idiot at home.

79
00:04:39,778 --> 00:04:41,242
You saw it yesterday too, right?

80
00:04:41,245 --> 00:04:43,338
How desperately those people
kept pressuring her.

81
00:04:44,838 --> 00:04:46,516
Please look after Ji Ni for me.

82
00:04:46,712 --> 00:04:48,009
Don't let her go anywhere.

83
00:04:48,011 --> 00:04:50,669
Especially don't let her go
anywhere near that hospital.

84
00:04:50,758 --> 00:04:52,692
Okay, I'm counting on you.

85
00:04:53,052 --> 00:04:55,681
Don't let your guard down.
Keep a close eye on her.

86
00:04:56,258 --> 00:04:58,589
Yeah, I'll be back soon.

87
00:04:58,654 --> 00:04:59,685
Okay. Yeah.

88
00:05:02,151 --> 00:05:03,161
What?

89
00:05:03,163 --> 00:05:06,827
I'm so worried that I want to cancel
everything and stay by your side.

90
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:09,235
Don't worry. I won't.

91
00:05:09,238 --> 00:05:10,559
How can I trust you?

92
00:05:10,725 --> 00:05:12,496
You're too soft-hearted,

93
00:05:12,524 --> 00:05:15,297
- you might fall for it again.
- I said I won't.

94
00:05:15,318 --> 00:05:17,208
Stop worrying and focus on your work.

95
00:05:18,132 --> 00:05:19,576
Don't forget.

96
00:05:19,685 --> 00:05:21,945
Remember how we lived
because of that woman.

97
00:05:22,998 --> 00:05:26,163
The fact that she wants a blood test
means she considers us family.

98
00:05:26,398 --> 00:05:29,575
But she turned her back on you
when you were just a child,

99
00:05:29,918 --> 00:05:32,854
and grabbed you by the collar,
tormenting you until you couldn't breathe,

100
00:05:32,856 --> 00:05:34,495
and now she wants our help?

101
00:05:34,511 --> 00:05:36,705
She has some nerve.

102
00:05:36,707 --> 00:05:37,717
Mom,

103
00:05:38,332 --> 00:05:40,090
I hate to say this,

104
00:05:40,552 --> 00:05:43,389
- but you keep forgetting something.
- What did I forget?

105
00:05:43,391 --> 00:05:45,061
You started all of this.

106
00:05:45,064 --> 00:05:46,404
You and dad.

107
00:05:46,778 --> 00:05:48,632
And that woman was the first victim.

108
00:05:49,925 --> 00:05:53,556
If your dad's bone marrow had matched,
he would've donated all he could.

109
00:05:54,415 --> 00:05:55,425
You little brat!

110
00:05:55,598 --> 00:05:58,320
Do you really have to point it out
like that?

111
00:05:58,512 --> 00:05:59,531
You awful girl!

112
00:05:59,638 --> 00:06:01,250
You're just like me.

113
00:06:01,252 --> 00:06:03,303
If I hate her, you should hate her too!

114
00:06:03,305 --> 00:06:05,090
A child isn't your clone.

115
00:06:05,764 --> 00:06:06,960
Anyway,

116
00:06:07,778 --> 00:06:10,336
I'll be back soon,
so don't go anywhere near that hospital.

117
00:06:10,338 --> 00:06:13,143
If you do anything stupid,
we're both dead!

118
00:06:13,318 --> 00:06:15,882
Don't say things that sound so scary.

119
00:06:16,057 --> 00:06:17,317
Listen carefully.

120
00:06:17,533 --> 00:06:20,079
I'm going to blow that place up.

121
00:06:20,238 --> 00:06:23,411
What they said to you,
what they did to me,

122
00:06:23,578 --> 00:06:27,243
whether it was that family or me,
I'll never forget it.

123
00:06:28,785 --> 00:06:31,036
Our families should never cross paths.

124
00:06:31,051 --> 00:06:33,801
They shouldn't even exist in this world.

125
00:06:33,824 --> 00:06:36,034
That's the only answer. Got it?

126
00:06:36,215 --> 00:06:38,652
- Do you understand?
- I understand.

127
00:06:38,654 --> 00:06:40,562
Just leave already.

128
00:06:42,705 --> 00:06:44,052
Don't follow me out.

129
00:06:54,658 --> 00:06:55,945
Dad,

130
00:06:56,170 --> 00:06:59,412
I'm so scared. What am I supposed to do?

131
00:07:02,676 --> 00:07:05,832
Please help me make sure
she never finds out.

132
00:07:06,218 --> 00:07:08,375
I'm really scared.

133
00:07:19,305 --> 00:07:20,575
Hello?

134
00:07:22,247 --> 00:07:23,434
Yes.

135
00:07:23,678 --> 00:07:25,389
Mom went to Indonesia.

136
00:07:25,532 --> 00:07:27,289
You know she runs my dad's business.

137
00:07:27,893 --> 00:07:28,922
Yes.

138
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:30,346
Really?

139
00:07:31,156 --> 00:07:32,968
That's a relief.

140
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:34,898
Yes.

141
00:07:35,452 --> 00:07:36,471
Please.

142
00:07:36,672 --> 00:07:38,593
It has to stay a secret.

143
00:07:39,658 --> 00:07:41,636
Otherwise, I'm really dead.

144
00:07:43,685 --> 00:07:44,686
Yes.

145
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:46,084
Okay, I understand.

146
00:08:00,172 --> 00:08:01,380
Mom.

147
00:08:05,645 --> 00:08:06,856
Is it true?

148
00:08:07,242 --> 00:08:10,214
Did you really find a bone marrow donor
for O Reum?

149
00:08:10,229 --> 00:08:11,561
Yes, ma'am.

150
00:08:11,912 --> 00:08:13,802
You can finally put your mind at ease.

151
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:14,938
How?

152
00:08:15,045 --> 00:08:17,975
We found an unrelated donor here in Korea.

153
00:08:18,205 --> 00:08:19,885
Let's prepare for the transplant.

154
00:08:20,178 --> 00:08:22,293
He'll undergo a week of conditioning...

155
00:08:22,499 --> 00:08:24,684
in the isolation room.

156
00:08:24,972 --> 00:08:27,392
You must have been very worried too.

157
00:08:27,979 --> 00:08:29,436
I was too.

158
00:08:29,569 --> 00:08:30,643
Yes.

159
00:08:32,511 --> 00:08:34,061
Tell Mai right away.

160
00:08:34,158 --> 00:08:36,618
She's still in the caregiver room, right?

161
00:08:38,232 --> 00:08:41,017
When can he leave the isolation room?

162
00:08:41,564 --> 00:08:43,161
She mentioned it earlier.

163
00:08:43,491 --> 00:08:45,140
He'd have a week of conditioning.

164
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:46,662
Yes, that's right.

165
00:08:46,792 --> 00:08:48,950
I know you're anxious,
but please wait a little longer.

166
00:08:48,952 --> 00:08:51,738
He's already been through
a long course of chemotherapy,

167
00:08:52,286 --> 00:08:53,777
so I'm sure he'll do well.

168
00:08:53,825 --> 00:08:58,481
- Okay, thank you.
- Thank you.

169
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:11,712
Really?

170
00:09:12,330 --> 00:09:13,479
Then,

171
00:09:13,519 --> 00:09:15,555
O Reum can live?

172
00:09:15,557 --> 00:09:17,642
Yes, that's what I'm saying.

173
00:09:18,690 --> 00:09:20,109
Really?

174
00:09:21,225 --> 00:09:23,950
Can he really survive?

175
00:09:23,952 --> 00:09:27,607
Yes. How many times are you going to ask?
I told you we found a donor.

176
00:09:27,991 --> 00:09:29,945
I just can't believe it.

177
00:09:37,585 --> 00:09:39,855
Why are you crying?

178
00:09:41,385 --> 00:09:43,901
Because I'm so happy.

179
00:09:44,043 --> 00:09:45,611
Don't cry.

180
00:09:53,485 --> 00:09:56,833
Yes, I just heard the news
from the doctor.

181
00:09:57,073 --> 00:09:58,686
I'm so happy.

182
00:09:59,038 --> 00:10:01,322
I wanted to tell you, Sa Bin.

183
00:10:02,092 --> 00:10:03,103
I mean...

184
00:10:03,105 --> 00:10:04,824
you're not family, but...

185
00:10:05,349 --> 00:10:07,636
you're someone who comforted me so much.

186
00:10:07,752 --> 00:10:09,858
Of course you should tell me.

187
00:10:10,072 --> 00:10:12,223
Do you know how much I've been waiting
and worrying?

188
00:10:12,225 --> 00:10:14,274
That's why I called you first.

189
00:10:15,185 --> 00:10:17,462
I'll never forget how you helped me...

190
00:10:17,582 --> 00:10:20,741
when I felt like giving up. Thank you.

191
00:10:22,131 --> 00:10:24,799
Then I'll go see my kids now.

192
00:10:24,909 --> 00:10:27,132
- See you later.
- Yes, take care.

193
00:10:46,718 --> 00:10:47,865
Yes.

194
00:10:49,575 --> 00:10:50,798
Sa Bin.

195
00:10:53,352 --> 00:10:55,142
Something good must've happened.

196
00:10:55,145 --> 00:10:57,079
I could hear you humming
all the way out here.

197
00:10:57,170 --> 00:10:58,379
Really?

198
00:10:59,005 --> 00:11:02,681
I went around all the shops yesterday
to inform them about the rent increase.

199
00:11:02,684 --> 00:11:04,668
I heard.
That must've been tough in this heat.

200
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:05,995
It was.

201
00:11:06,085 --> 00:11:09,060
Still, it's a building
I recommended you buy,

202
00:11:09,062 --> 00:11:10,645
so I figured I should help out.

203
00:11:10,647 --> 00:11:12,798
- You know the rent went up a lot, right?
- Of course.

204
00:11:13,192 --> 00:11:16,055
Neither my brother nor I know much
about this stuff,

205
00:11:16,316 --> 00:11:18,518
but thanks to you
I became building owners.

206
00:11:18,605 --> 00:11:20,258
You should tell your brother.

207
00:11:20,338 --> 00:11:22,807
He acts like he's the only one
making money.

208
00:11:22,809 --> 00:11:24,133
He knows.

209
00:11:24,870 --> 00:11:26,043
But Sun Kyung,

210
00:11:26,046 --> 00:11:27,754
this time,

211
00:11:28,474 --> 00:11:30,922
- I'm thinking of freezing the rent.
- What?

212
00:11:32,256 --> 00:11:35,071
If you freeze it now,
it'll be locked for years.

213
00:11:35,212 --> 00:11:37,402
- Do you know what that means?
- I do.

214
00:11:37,651 --> 00:11:40,925
But we've all become like family
in that building.

215
00:11:41,333 --> 00:11:43,216
Knowing how hard things are for them,

216
00:11:43,295 --> 00:11:46,945
- it just doesn't feel right to raise it.
- That's why I play the bad guy.

217
00:11:46,947 --> 00:11:48,628
You can just pretend you don't know...

218
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:51,483
I won't pretend. I'll tell them myself.

219
00:11:51,485 --> 00:11:54,132
And I'll dip into my savings
and pay for the repairs.

220
00:11:54,265 --> 00:11:55,727
Why all of a sudden?

221
00:11:56,772 --> 00:11:58,348
Are you upset with me about something?

222
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:00,651
No, nothing like that.

223
00:12:01,111 --> 00:12:03,029
It's just how I feel.

224
00:12:03,318 --> 00:12:07,002
It's not like I have kids in college
like other people,

225
00:12:07,501 --> 00:12:10,512
so there's nothing wrong
with helping others a little.

226
00:12:10,571 --> 00:12:11,962
Is this about the singing class?

227
00:12:11,965 --> 00:12:14,862
You got attached while going there, right?

228
00:12:15,678 --> 00:12:17,822
And it's not like you learned singing
for free either.

229
00:12:18,819 --> 00:12:20,223
Yes, that's part of it too.

230
00:12:20,225 --> 00:12:22,536
Sorry I didn't bring it up sooner.

231
00:12:22,538 --> 00:12:24,641
This isn't right.

232
00:12:25,331 --> 00:12:27,098
Seriously.

233
00:12:29,285 --> 00:12:32,585
You shouldn't wash that yet.

234
00:12:32,593 --> 00:12:35,614
There's a bit of a stain right here.

235
00:12:35,617 --> 00:12:38,040
It's okay, I'll wash it later.

236
00:12:38,043 --> 00:12:39,223
Okay.

237
00:12:40,044 --> 00:12:41,805
That's really weird.

238
00:12:43,931 --> 00:12:45,744
You're acting strange.

239
00:12:58,557 --> 00:13:00,824
(K-content exports expand,
accelerating global market growth)

240
00:13:11,912 --> 00:13:15,122
No matter how hard they try,
nothing beats a printed newspaper.

241
00:13:16,718 --> 00:13:19,078
Come on. It's a digital world now.

242
00:13:19,545 --> 00:13:21,998
You and your brother
are both so old-fashioned.

243
00:13:22,634 --> 00:13:23,700
What brought this on all of a sudden?

244
00:13:23,702 --> 00:13:26,042
He says he's going
to freeze the building rent.

245
00:13:26,470 --> 00:13:28,578
Good for him.
What's the point of raising it?

246
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,011
He doesn't have kids in college,

247
00:13:30,013 --> 00:13:32,703
no kids to marry off, and he's definitely
not getting married himself.

248
00:13:32,991 --> 00:13:36,296
See? You talk exactly the same.

249
00:13:36,298 --> 00:13:37,909
Who do you think set all this up?

250
00:13:37,947 --> 00:13:40,026
And now you're acting generous with it?

251
00:13:40,052 --> 00:13:41,544
You're the one who set it up.

252
00:13:41,546 --> 00:13:43,863
- You know that.
- Yeah, I do, so drop it.

253
00:13:47,045 --> 00:13:49,527
- Something's off with Sa Bin.
- What now?

254
00:13:49,851 --> 00:13:53,191
There's a stain all over his shirt,

255
00:13:53,518 --> 00:13:55,373
- but he won't wash it.
- Is that strange?

256
00:13:55,467 --> 00:13:58,294
You know those obsessed fans?

257
00:13:58,538 --> 00:14:02,206
The ones who treasure even tissues
their idol has used?

258
00:14:02,394 --> 00:14:04,028
It's exactly like that.

259
00:14:04,285 --> 00:14:05,399
Someone...

260
00:14:05,527 --> 00:14:09,153
got his shirt all stained,
and he won't wash it.

261
00:14:09,367 --> 00:14:10,850
And this morning,

262
00:14:11,114 --> 00:14:13,752
he was even humming to himself.
Weird, right?

263
00:14:14,018 --> 00:14:16,800
That cellist just became a widow.
You think something's going on?

264
00:14:16,802 --> 00:14:18,505
No way.

265
00:14:18,531 --> 00:14:19,532
Why not?

266
00:14:19,552 --> 00:14:22,573
After 20 years of marriage,
I'm finally getting a sister-in-law,

267
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,678
and I hate women who are that impressive.

268
00:14:25,825 --> 00:14:28,177
And I'm the one who built this wealth,

269
00:14:28,232 --> 00:14:30,598
just for some other woman to come in
and enjoy it?

270
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:32,668
Sa Bin pays a lot for living expenses.

271
00:14:32,672 --> 00:14:35,285
And what do you mean
"you built this wealth?"

272
00:14:35,369 --> 00:14:37,372
He spent every day brewing medicine...

273
00:14:37,374 --> 00:14:38,888
at his senior's clinic to earn that money.

274
00:14:39,171 --> 00:14:40,177
He just opened his own clinic.

275
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:43,204
I made him snacks through all that,

276
00:14:43,206 --> 00:14:46,051
- so who really took care of him?
- Well...

277
00:14:46,273 --> 00:14:48,124
- The housekeeper.
- What?

278
00:14:49,466 --> 00:14:51,674
Okay, let's eat breakfast.

279
00:14:58,285 --> 00:14:59,285
Really?

280
00:15:02,245 --> 00:15:03,286
We're saved.

281
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:06,105
He's going to make it.

282
00:15:08,345 --> 00:15:09,791
That's a relief, Seung Woo.

283
00:15:10,171 --> 00:15:12,991
That's amazing news.

284
00:15:14,139 --> 00:15:15,292
Me?

285
00:15:15,698 --> 00:15:17,198
I've got two job interviews today.

286
00:15:19,052 --> 00:15:22,071
I bragged to mom that I'd get a job
within ten days.

287
00:15:22,477 --> 00:15:26,192
Seung Woo, be nicer to mom.

288
00:15:27,058 --> 00:15:28,592
There's no mother like mom.

289
00:15:28,925 --> 00:15:30,490
No woman like her, either.

290
00:15:30,957 --> 00:15:31,984
Got it?

291
00:15:33,585 --> 00:15:34,618
Yeah.

292
00:15:42,805 --> 00:15:44,165
My dear O Reum...

293
00:15:47,192 --> 00:15:48,550
Thank you.

294
00:15:50,505 --> 00:15:51,709
Thank you.

295
00:16:00,338 --> 00:16:02,985
I made you some herbal tea, have a little.

296
00:16:06,938 --> 00:16:09,094
So now you finally see me?

297
00:16:09,595 --> 00:16:10,891
I'm sorry.

298
00:16:12,112 --> 00:16:13,956
I really wasn't in my right mind.

299
00:16:14,336 --> 00:16:15,633
I understand.

300
00:16:16,452 --> 00:16:18,211
When your child is going through that,

301
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:20,991
what parent could stay sane?

302
00:16:22,445 --> 00:16:24,450
Thank you for understanding, Mom.

303
00:16:25,698 --> 00:16:26,983
I'm sorry.

304
00:16:27,545 --> 00:16:29,254
I'm just relieved it got resolved...

305
00:16:29,295 --> 00:16:31,071
without relying on Ji Ni.

306
00:16:32,185 --> 00:16:35,577
Even when I went back yesterday
to apologize and beg,

307
00:16:36,465 --> 00:16:38,505
She asked me,
"If the marrow turns out to match,

308
00:16:38,730 --> 00:16:41,877
will your whole family come after us?"

309
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:44,442
I had nothing to say.

310
00:16:44,872 --> 00:16:46,588
I figured as much.

311
00:16:47,275 --> 00:16:51,185
At that point, I would've clung to her
even more desperately.

312
00:16:54,938 --> 00:16:56,804
I'm just glad there's a donor.

313
00:16:56,898 --> 00:16:58,475
Our dear O Reum...

314
00:16:59,290 --> 00:17:00,798
he's a lucky kid.

315
00:17:03,241 --> 00:17:04,334
Mom.

316
00:17:09,058 --> 00:17:11,885
These are sample question cards
to include with the storybook.

317
00:17:12,892 --> 00:17:14,985
After kids finish reading,

318
00:17:15,086 --> 00:17:17,169
they pull a card from the pocket...

319
00:17:17,310 --> 00:17:18,578
and play a question game.

320
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,896
"What if Patjwi had been kind?"

321
00:17:21,964 --> 00:17:25,294
"What if the toad hadn't helped Kongjwi?"

322
00:17:26,035 --> 00:17:27,205
Nice.

323
00:17:28,012 --> 00:17:29,348
You came up with this at the hospital?

324
00:17:29,395 --> 00:17:30,887
- Is it okay?
- Yeah.

325
00:17:33,618 --> 00:17:35,673
Your mom still doesn't know, right?

326
00:17:35,768 --> 00:17:37,092
What do you mean "still?"

327
00:17:37,192 --> 00:17:38,672
She can never find out.

328
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:41,954
Look, I'm getting chills.
It's honestly scary.

329
00:17:41,998 --> 00:17:44,078
Even this morning,
on her way to Indonesia,

330
00:17:44,145 --> 00:17:46,565
she was so intimidating about it.

331
00:17:46,678 --> 00:17:49,085
Actually, I got a call too.

332
00:17:49,112 --> 00:17:50,792
- From my mom?
- Yeah.

333
00:17:52,058 --> 00:17:53,872
I think she got my number from Jung A.

334
00:17:53,932 --> 00:17:57,382
She told me to keep checking
that you don't go to the hospital,

335
00:17:57,543 --> 00:17:59,466
and that you go straight home after work.

336
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:02,178
I swear, this is exhausting.

337
00:18:03,172 --> 00:18:05,085
Jung A and I are nervous now too.

338
00:18:12,712 --> 00:18:14,004
What about Jeon Jung A?

339
00:18:14,127 --> 00:18:15,692
She didn't make it past the final round.

340
00:18:17,258 --> 00:18:19,290
I liked her work, though.

341
00:18:19,858 --> 00:18:21,605
It's soft, comforting, and warm.

342
00:18:21,646 --> 00:18:23,506
But I guess the professors
preferred something darker,

343
00:18:23,521 --> 00:18:26,458
with a clearer, stronger theme.

344
00:18:26,692 --> 00:18:28,291
She seemed to have high expectations.

345
00:18:28,391 --> 00:18:30,954
This is why you shouldn't get personally
involved with artists.

346
00:18:31,145 --> 00:18:32,172
It just hurts too much.

347
00:18:32,272 --> 00:18:34,678
It can't be helped. It's not in our hands.

348
00:18:40,365 --> 00:18:42,576
We shouldn't be worrying
about Jung A right now.

349
00:18:43,098 --> 00:18:44,676
I made a lot of misjudgments.

350
00:18:45,217 --> 00:18:46,400
No, that's not true.

351
00:18:49,032 --> 00:18:50,467
So, here's my thought.

352
00:18:50,814 --> 00:18:52,439
What if we held an exhibition...

353
00:18:52,494 --> 00:18:54,258
for the submitted artworks this time?

354
00:18:54,505 --> 00:18:57,578
I'd like to at least give the artists
a chance to present their work.

355
00:18:57,706 --> 00:18:58,885
Am I overstepping?

356
00:18:59,051 --> 00:19:01,992
I'd like to hear your opinions,
since you've been here longer than I have.

357
00:19:02,186 --> 00:19:03,311
I'm in favor.

358
00:19:03,416 --> 00:19:04,745
Me too.

359
00:19:04,878 --> 00:19:07,878
Our artists have worked really hard.

360
00:19:08,032 --> 00:19:09,038
Right.

361
00:19:09,372 --> 00:19:11,284
That's something we can do for them.

362
00:19:12,282 --> 00:19:13,989
How about a month in the center lobby?

363
00:19:14,591 --> 00:19:15,979
That might be too long.

364
00:19:16,032 --> 00:19:17,932
Let's plan for a ten-day exhibition.

365
00:19:18,032 --> 00:19:19,816
Sounds good. I'll draft the proposal.

366
00:19:20,392 --> 00:19:21,977
What should we have for lunch?

367
00:19:22,385 --> 00:19:24,223
You two go ahead. I have plans.

368
00:19:24,225 --> 00:19:25,225
Okay.

369
00:19:29,938 --> 00:19:31,037
That's not it.

370
00:19:31,039 --> 00:19:32,902
It's clearly a desk.
Doesn't it look like one?

371
00:19:32,956 --> 00:19:35,515
No, look closely.
I told you, it's a chair.

372
00:19:35,687 --> 00:19:36,848
It was made wrong.

373
00:19:37,878 --> 00:19:39,836
They've been at it since earlier.

374
00:19:39,952 --> 00:19:42,760
They said they'd make a storybook,
but now they're opening a preschool.

375
00:19:43,858 --> 00:19:45,148
What would you like to drink?

376
00:19:45,951 --> 00:19:48,054
Forget drinks. Has everyone eaten?

377
00:19:48,772 --> 00:19:50,365
I think they're ordering pizza.

378
00:19:55,205 --> 00:19:56,888
You immature publishers,

379
00:19:56,955 --> 00:19:58,977
you said you came for lunch,
but you haven't ordered anything.

380
00:19:58,979 --> 00:20:00,387
You're just hogging the table.

381
00:20:00,511 --> 00:20:01,574
I could sue you for this.

382
00:20:01,661 --> 00:20:03,370
Right, pizza.

383
00:20:04,078 --> 00:20:05,692
- You're here?
- I'm here.

384
00:20:06,473 --> 00:20:09,212
- How are you doing now?
- Better, thanks to you.

385
00:20:09,278 --> 00:20:11,695
We ordered pizza.

386
00:20:11,909 --> 00:20:13,651
- Do you want to eat with us?
- Sure.

387
00:20:13,678 --> 00:20:14,908
Then I'll go get drinks.

388
00:20:15,045 --> 00:20:16,287
Water is fine for me.

389
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:18,169
Each person must order at least one item.

390
00:20:18,172 --> 00:20:19,656
I have rent to pay, you know.

391
00:20:19,659 --> 00:20:21,888
- Get me an iced Americano.
- I'll order.

392
00:20:26,375 --> 00:20:27,985
Can we talk for a moment?

393
00:20:31,492 --> 00:20:34,083
I didn't expect much,
but I still had my hopes up.

394
00:20:34,265 --> 00:20:36,769
I'm sorry. It wasn't my decision to make.

395
00:20:37,674 --> 00:20:39,011
I understand.

396
00:20:39,558 --> 00:20:40,678
Is that why you came in person?

397
00:20:40,732 --> 00:20:42,976
It'll be posted on the website tomorrow.

398
00:20:43,064 --> 00:20:44,598
I didn't want you to find out that way.

399
00:20:45,145 --> 00:20:46,984
You helped me a lot when I needed it.

400
00:20:47,292 --> 00:20:48,496
Thank you.

401
00:20:49,672 --> 00:20:52,189
I'll make a fortune with this café.

402
00:20:52,192 --> 00:20:54,171
I'll buy all the great paintings
in the world,

403
00:20:54,212 --> 00:20:56,291
- and say I painted them all.
- What?

404
00:20:58,238 --> 00:21:01,382
Your unique charm
seems to show in your paintings.

405
00:21:01,803 --> 00:21:03,830
- Really?
- Absolutely.

406
00:21:05,572 --> 00:21:06,992
Your paintings are nice, Jung A.

407
00:21:07,185 --> 00:21:09,394
More good things will come your way
after this contest.

408
00:21:09,462 --> 00:21:11,048
What do you like about them?

409
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:13,885
They're warm and bright.

410
00:21:14,238 --> 00:21:15,485
Because the artist is bright.

411
00:21:16,385 --> 00:21:17,985
I needed to hear that.

412
00:21:18,052 --> 00:21:20,585
That gives me so much courage. Thank you.

413
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,622
No one knows yet, right?

414
00:21:23,625 --> 00:21:24,909
Especially Ji Ni or Tae O.

415
00:21:24,970 --> 00:21:25,971
Not yet.

416
00:21:26,465 --> 00:21:28,578
You're the first person I've told
besides our staff.

417
00:21:30,291 --> 00:21:31,978
Please don't tell anyone yet.

418
00:21:33,016 --> 00:21:34,838
I'm not ready for people to comfort me.

419
00:21:34,992 --> 00:21:36,692
I'll tell them myself later.

420
00:21:36,867 --> 00:21:37,955
Okay.

421
00:21:39,390 --> 00:21:41,959
Let's go back in.
I think the pizza is here.

422
00:21:42,013 --> 00:21:43,065
Okay, let's go.

423
00:21:45,285 --> 00:21:47,604
Here comes the pizza.

424
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:50,495
I'm starving.

425
00:21:51,661 --> 00:21:53,572
- Pizza's here.
- Let's set it up.

426
00:22:01,871 --> 00:22:03,185
Done.

427
00:22:21,703 --> 00:22:23,283
Selling paintings isn't easy.

428
00:22:23,332 --> 00:22:24,818
People only buy them as investments.

429
00:22:24,885 --> 00:22:26,079
Should I buy some?

430
00:22:26,365 --> 00:22:28,285
We expanded the publishing house.
We can hang them there.

431
00:22:29,492 --> 00:22:32,016
You sound like you did when I was nine,
offering to buy me a robot.

432
00:22:53,352 --> 00:22:55,471
- Did Professor Bae write this?
- No.

433
00:22:56,745 --> 00:22:57,758
Yes.

434
00:22:58,971 --> 00:23:01,385
I wrote it, and Professor Bae approved it.

435
00:23:04,465 --> 00:23:07,350
A complete family, flaws and all.

436
00:23:07,555 --> 00:23:10,445
Nice wording. Good work.

437
00:23:27,038 --> 00:23:28,466
I'm back.

438
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,874
Why do you look so down?

439
00:23:30,989 --> 00:23:32,902
- Is it because it's hot?
- No.

440
00:23:33,042 --> 00:23:34,878
- Dinner?
- I'm fine.

441
00:23:35,032 --> 00:23:36,659
I'll get something later if I need to.

442
00:23:37,102 --> 00:23:38,138
Ma'am?

443
00:23:38,141 --> 00:23:39,985
We don't need anything either.

444
00:23:42,112 --> 00:23:43,291
He'll like it, right?

445
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:49,491
Stay here. I'm worried.

446
00:23:49,532 --> 00:23:50,834
Then you should've stopped her.

447
00:23:50,849 --> 00:23:53,185
- I told you I didn't know.
- Let her handle it herself.

448
00:24:05,825 --> 00:24:07,044
What do you think?

449
00:24:07,059 --> 00:24:09,092
It's my surprise.

450
00:24:10,672 --> 00:24:13,685
- You bought this?
- Yes. Aren't I sweet?

451
00:24:13,927 --> 00:24:17,125
I emptied my mom's wallet just for you.

452
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:19,173
Her future son-in-law's first project...

453
00:24:19,175 --> 00:24:20,460
couldn't be left to fail...

454
00:24:20,885 --> 00:24:23,922
No, it's not failing.

455
00:24:24,003 --> 00:24:26,478
But I had to lift your spirits.

456
00:24:26,516 --> 00:24:29,850
Mom said, "Fine," and handed me her card.

457
00:24:30,495 --> 00:24:31,745
Dad being sick was just an excuse...

458
00:24:31,798 --> 00:24:33,583
So that's why you went to England?

459
00:24:33,724 --> 00:24:34,843
Don't you like it?

460
00:24:34,912 --> 00:24:37,827
Dad being sick wasn't a lie.
That was true too.

461
00:24:41,078 --> 00:24:42,149
Ji Hu...

462
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:44,637
You really don't know me.

463
00:24:44,678 --> 00:24:46,957
What is it now?

464
00:24:47,080 --> 00:24:48,100
"What now?"

465
00:24:51,878 --> 00:24:54,411
Anyway, thank you.
I appreciate the thought.

466
00:24:55,672 --> 00:24:58,105
Why only the thought?
You should accept the painting too.

467
00:24:58,192 --> 00:25:01,264
It's underrated now,
but it'll draw attention later.

468
00:25:01,872 --> 00:25:03,692
My mom buys art, you know.

469
00:25:03,798 --> 00:25:05,345
Her predictions are never wrong.

470
00:25:06,291 --> 00:25:09,372
You like this painting
because of what your mom said?

471
00:25:10,038 --> 00:25:11,452
You're an artist.

472
00:25:11,545 --> 00:25:12,618
Is that all you can say?

473
00:25:12,738 --> 00:25:15,285
What are you upset about now?

474
00:25:15,712 --> 00:25:18,692
You displayed a great painting,
but people didn't recognize it.

475
00:25:18,865 --> 00:25:20,195
Then someone who did...

476
00:25:20,243 --> 00:25:23,271
turned out to be my mom
and bought it. Is that so bad?

477
00:25:23,332 --> 00:25:25,166
You get recognition,

478
00:25:25,207 --> 00:25:27,192
and my mom gets a good painting
at a low price.

479
00:25:27,265 --> 00:25:28,597
Everyone wins, right?

480
00:25:30,275 --> 00:25:31,530
Let's talk later.

481
00:25:32,325 --> 00:25:33,638
Are you just telling me to go?

482
00:25:36,092 --> 00:25:37,498
Not even a thank-you kiss?

483
00:25:37,571 --> 00:25:40,972
"Thanks for caring about me
when I was struggling."

484
00:25:41,312 --> 00:25:42,892
"Let's call my future mother-in-law."

485
00:25:43,405 --> 00:25:45,585
Isn't that how this should go?

486
00:25:51,311 --> 00:25:53,120
I don't even know what to say.

487
00:25:53,138 --> 00:25:54,792
Our values are too different.

488
00:25:55,051 --> 00:25:56,445
I can see that too.

489
00:25:57,478 --> 00:25:58,878
How did you even date her?

490
00:25:59,212 --> 00:26:00,778
She wasn't like that in England.

491
00:26:01,072 --> 00:26:03,379
She likes luxury brands
and posting photos,

492
00:26:03,517 --> 00:26:05,165
but girls her age are all like that.

493
00:26:05,212 --> 00:26:06,832
Life while studying abroad is simple.

494
00:26:06,858 --> 00:26:09,378
You study, take exams,
and that's about it.

495
00:26:11,612 --> 00:26:12,631
Right.

496
00:26:13,232 --> 00:26:14,540
The decision is yours.

497
00:26:15,698 --> 00:26:18,152
From what I can see,
you have very firm boundaries,

498
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:21,578
but Do Hee and your future in-laws
are very materialistic.

499
00:26:21,655 --> 00:26:23,744
Of course, I'm on your side
because you're my son,

500
00:26:24,691 --> 00:26:26,696
but your mom and Do Hee
might see it differently.

501
00:26:27,490 --> 00:26:28,531
What should I do?

502
00:26:28,585 --> 00:26:31,479
What matters is how much you love her.

503
00:26:31,565 --> 00:26:33,051
The person who loves more gives in.

504
00:26:33,053 --> 00:26:34,592
You accept it all and keep going.

505
00:26:38,245 --> 00:26:40,069
How much do you love Do Hee?

506
00:26:40,625 --> 00:26:43,005
Things like this will keep happening.

507
00:26:46,238 --> 00:26:48,834
Mother, what did I do wrong?

508
00:26:49,185 --> 00:26:51,291
I just can't understand.

509
00:26:51,472 --> 00:26:53,985
Other women couldn't help
even if they wanted to.

510
00:26:54,145 --> 00:26:56,157
Not everyone can do something like this.

511
00:26:56,185 --> 00:26:57,398
Exactly.

512
00:26:57,458 --> 00:26:59,298
Your mother made a very generous gesture.

513
00:26:59,418 --> 00:27:01,878
Then why is he acting that way?

514
00:27:02,445 --> 00:27:03,683
I thought...

515
00:27:03,773 --> 00:27:05,160
he'd be showering me
with affection tonight.

516
00:27:05,162 --> 00:27:06,169
Am I wrong?

517
00:27:06,172 --> 00:27:07,652
Exactly my point.

518
00:27:08,392 --> 00:27:10,376
He wasn't like this back in England.

519
00:27:10,392 --> 00:27:12,578
Ji Hu is getting stranger every day.

520
00:27:14,125 --> 00:27:15,791
He really must be crazy.

521
00:27:15,938 --> 00:27:17,282
Isn't he crazy?

522
00:27:17,349 --> 00:27:18,885
He is.

523
00:27:18,958 --> 00:27:21,070
Others would be desperate
for a chance like this,

524
00:27:21,151 --> 00:27:23,893
so how can he react like that?

525
00:27:25,192 --> 00:27:27,678
Still, watch how you speak.

526
00:27:27,978 --> 00:27:29,776
Am I your birth mother?

527
00:27:31,330 --> 00:27:33,425
Right. You're my mother-in-law.

528
00:27:33,427 --> 00:27:34,430
I'm sorry.

529
00:27:34,432 --> 00:27:35,885
I was just so mad.

530
00:27:36,232 --> 00:27:39,172
Does your mother let you speak like that?

531
00:27:39,252 --> 00:27:41,185
My mom is even worse...

532
00:27:43,338 --> 00:27:45,285
She stays quiet when Dad is around.

533
00:27:45,352 --> 00:27:48,190
Mom and I only talk like that
when we're alone.

534
00:27:49,811 --> 00:27:50,992
Go home today.

535
00:27:51,158 --> 00:27:53,492
Ji Hu seems to have a lot on his mind.

536
00:27:58,232 --> 00:28:01,192
This is so annoying.
I spent all that money for this?

537
00:28:21,395 --> 00:28:24,753
(Family Register)

538
00:28:24,756 --> 00:28:26,936
O Reum's lifesaver?

539
00:28:26,938 --> 00:28:28,219
I was older than you,

540
00:28:28,221 --> 00:28:30,278
but not as mature as you are now.

541
00:28:30,378 --> 00:28:32,997
This is the first secret
I've ever kept from my mom.

542
00:28:33,052 --> 00:28:34,438
Did you take care of what I asked?

543
00:28:34,452 --> 00:28:35,462
Make sure you go too.

544
00:28:35,464 --> 00:28:37,192
- Honeymoon?
- Did you meet someone?

545
00:28:37,198 --> 00:28:38,485
After just one week without me?

546
00:28:38,491 --> 00:28:40,192
How could you do this to me?

547
00:28:40,194 --> 00:28:43,405
- Is there another woman?
- My heart's wavering. It really is.

548
00:28:44,664 --> 00:28:46,759
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
